# BuildKit reads the ignore file next to the Dockerfile first, before the one at
# the context root. That is why this file exists at all: the build context for
# the site image is web/, and the root .dockerignore - the one that excludes web/
# from the Go image's context - is not consulted from there.
#
# Without this, a local `npm install` or `npm run build` would be uploaded as
# part of the context and `COPY . .` would land the host's node_modules (macOS
# binaries, if you are on a Mac) on top of the ones `npm ci` just installed in
# the image. The build would still succeed and the nightly site build would then
# fail for reasons that make no sense from inside the cluster.
node_modules
dist
.astro
.output
.cache
.vite
*.log
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
